  "notes": "{当|あ}たる is a highly polysemous intransitive verb. The core idea is \"something comes into contact or alignment.\"\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Pair: {当|あ}てる (transitive — to hit something, to guess correctly)\n\nKEY USES:\n1. TO HIT: ボールが{頭|あたま}に{当|あ}たる (ball hits the head)\n2. TO WIN: くじに{当|あ}たる (to win a lottery)\n3. TO BE CORRECT: {予想|よそう}が{当|あ}たる (prediction comes true)\n4. TO APPLY TO: 〜に{当|あ}たる (to correspond to, to fall under)\n5. TO BE EXPOSED: {日|ひ}に{当|あ}たる (to be exposed to sunlight)\n\nRELATED:\n- {当|あ}たり: a hit, success (noun)\n- {当|あ}たり{前|まえ}: natural, obvious\n- {当|あ}たり{外|はず}れ: hit or miss",
